              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "fastīdium, fastīdiī — \"disgust, squeamishness; disdain\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Aeger cibum cum fastīdiō spectat. The sick man looks at the food with disgust."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter, second declension. Disgust of the stomach, and the scorn of a snob."
            }
          ]
        },
